<p><b>Type:</b> Icon, side. <b>Signature:</b> the season colour (<code>--im-poster-tint</code>) and the pixel episode number. A new season gets a new tint and keeps everything else, so the playlist reads as one show in stripes of colour.</p>

<h2 id="project-log">Project log</h2>
{{#example code=false}}
<div class="im-grid-auto im-grid-md">
	<figure class="im-poster im-poster-screen">
		<strong class="im-poster-word">it finally works<i class="im-poster-dot"></i></strong>
		<div class="im-poster-screen-frame"><img src="/assets/photos/desk-coffee.jpg" alt=""></div>
		<span class="im-poster-chip im-poster-chip-ink">log 07</span>
		<img class="im-poster-subject im-poster-card" src="/assets/photos/hands-camera.jpg" alt="">
		<span class="im-poster-time">16:12</span>
	</figure>
	<figure class="im-poster im-poster-screen">
		<strong class="im-poster-word">I broke it again<i class="im-poster-dot"></i></strong>
		<div class="im-poster-screen-frame"><img src="/assets/photos/desk-notebook.jpg" alt=""></div>
		<span class="im-poster-chip im-poster-chip-ink">log 08</span>
		<img class="im-poster-subject im-poster-card" src="/assets/photos/person-coat.jpg" alt="">
		<span class="im-poster-time">21:37</span>
	</figure>
	<figure class="im-poster im-poster-number">
		<span class="im-poster-figure">100</span>
		<strong class="im-poster-word">days of building</strong>
		<img class="im-poster-subject im-poster-card" src="/assets/photos/desk-hands.jpg" alt="">
		<span class="im-poster-time">29:03</span>
	</figure>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p><b>Type:</b> Screen + face, with a Number for milestones. <b>Chip:</b> <code>log N</code>, ink. <b>Signature:</b> the ink chip — it is the only series with a black chip, so it reads as "work" in a feed of red. The word is what happened, in the first person, as it felt: "I broke it again" beats "debugging session".</p>

<h2 id="skit">Skit &amp; commentary</h2>
{{#example code=false}}
<div class="im-grid-auto im-grid-md">
	<figure class="im-poster im-poster-face">
		<img class="im-poster-subject im-poster-card" src="/assets/photos/lion-stare.jpg" alt="">
		<span class="im-poster-sticker">wait what</span>
		<strong class="im-poster-word">group<br>project<i class="im-poster-dot"></i></strong>
		<span class="im-poster-hand">every. single. time.</span>
		<span class="im-poster-time">04:20</span>
	</figure>
	<figure class="im-poster im-poster-versus">
		<img class="im-poster-media" src="/assets/photos/pug-blanket.jpg" alt="">
		<img class="im-poster-media" src="/assets/photos/person-hiker.jpg" alt="">
		<span class="im-poster-chip im-poster-chip-paper">me</span>
		<span class="im-poster-chip im-poster-chip-paper im-poster-chip-end">also me</span>
		<span class="im-poster-disc">vs</span>
		<strong class="im-poster-word im-poster-on-media">monday plans</strong>
		<span class="im-poster-time">03:11</span>
	</figure>
	<figure class="im-poster im-poster-type">
		<strong class="im-poster-word">nobody<br>reads the<br>manual<i class="im-poster-dot"></i></strong>
		<span class="im-poster-sticker">hot take</span>
		<span class="im-poster-time">07:45</span>
	</figure>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p><b>Type:</b> any, but the <b>sticker</b> is the signature — tilted, white-edged, two or three words. This is the one series allowed to be loud. It still uses one red, one sticker, one word block; loud is the <em>words</em>, not the number of things on the frame.</p>

